Hello,

OpenRADIUS 0.9.7 has just been released. The most important feature of
this release is SQL support.

This is implemented using a Perl module that can query any database
supported by DBI/DBD. The module supports arbitrary SQL statements and
bind variables. Data sets resulting from queries can be returned to
OpenRADIUS as reply A/V pairs, or can be used by the module as check
items for received A/V pairs.

An example schema for MySQL and a configuration- and behaviour file are
included.

See the full changelog at 
http://www.openradius.net/download/openradius-0.9.7/CHANGELOG

The source is at
http://www.openradius.net/download/openradius-0.9.7.tar.gz

Kind regards,


Emile van Bergen.

