Hello,

as a result of the trademark charge by the trademark holder
to Asterix and Obelix against my site MobiliX (UniX on
Mobile Devices) (see http://tuxmobil.org/mobilix_asterix.html )
I had to withdraw the domain mobilix.org in February 2003.

Looking for a new name I found many websites which expressed
Linux and included words for mobility in their domain names.

Some of these websites do not seem to offer any
content related to Linux.  Often their names are just
variations of the famous site Linux-on-Laptops by
Kenneth E. Harker. (see http://linux-on-laptops.com )

You can find domains which simply include keywords
of the plural form or replace the word laptop with
"notebook". Some just add "mobile" attributes.
You may find a detailed list in my article at 
TuxMobil http://tuxmobil.org/domain_grabbing.html

The article contains also a research about the usage
of Linux trademarks.

Werner

